 ### 3.6 Sampling
 
-Denoising diffusion implicit model (DDIM) sampling (Song *et al.*, 2021) with 50 steps and $\eta = 0$. We start from independent standard Gaussian noise on the lattice and on the (un-wrapped) coordinates, then alternate the standard DDIM update on each channel. Coordinates are wrapped to $[0,1)$ after every step. Predicted lattice parameters are de-standardised at the end and clipped to physically valid ranges $(a,b,c) \in [0.5, 100]$ Å, $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma) \in [10°, 170°]$ before being passed to `pymatgen.Lattice.from_parameters`.
+Denoising diffusion implicit model (DDIM) sampling (Song *et al.*, 2021) with 50 steps and $\eta = 0$. We start from independent standard Gaussian noise on the lattice and on the (un-wrapped) coordinates, then alternate the standard DDIM update on each channel. Coordinates are wrapped to $[0,1)$ after every step. Predicted lattice parameters are de-standardised at the end and clipped to physically valid ranges $(a,b,c) \in [0.5, 100]$ Å, $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma) \in [10°, 170°]$ before being passed to `pymatgen.Lattice.from_parameters`. In the learned-head mode the distance features at each step are computed in the current sample $\boldsymbol{\ell}^{(t)}$, clipped to the same ranges, and no reference cell enters sampling. A regression test (`tests/test_r2_fixes.py`) confirms that the sampled structures are bit-identical whatever cell is passed to the sampler in this mode, including an all-NaN one.
+
+When a cell is given (the oracle, the indexer control, a substituted head), the lattice channel is not sampled. At every step it is set to the forward-noised given cell, $\boldsymbol{\ell}^{(t)} \sim q(\boldsymbol{\ell}^{(t)} \mid \boldsymbol{\ell}_\text{given})$, so that the distance features and the lattice input see the same noise statistics as in training, and the given cell is the output lattice.
 
 A subtle bug fix is worth noting. In the x₀-residual variant, recovering the implicit ε for the DDIM update requires dividing by $\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}(t)}$; near $t = 0$ this denominator vanishes. We clamp it to 0.05 and skip the very last DDIM step when sampling, which removed a class of structures with NaN coordinates that we initially saw.
 
